Scope: {{ONE_LINE_SCOPE — e.g. "Shared product workspace for the <team/product>, Nava-primary."}}

## Boundaries

- {{What belongs here.}}
- Do not add code checkouts, credentials, `.env` files, `op://` URIs, tokens, or OS metadata to this workspace. Cloned repos live outside it and are referenced by path.
- {{Any material that needs review before sharing — e.g. client-sensitive, internal-only. Ask before moving, summarizing, or sharing it.}}
- Nearest, most-specific `AGENTS.md` wins for local decisions, unless it conflicts with this authority boundary.

## Layout

- `product-work/` — shared product work the team relies on. One folder per product area; each declares one Context Fabric profile. (Rename this lane if your team prefers another name.)
- `prototyping/` — spikes, mockups, and experiments. No assigned profile.
- `agentic-support/` — the support layer: reusable skills and shared context. (Add at Walk phase.)

## Where things live

- Reusable procedures: `agentic-support/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` (the source of truth). Do not duplicate them in product folders.
- Shared facts (systems, repos, product profiles): `agentic-support/context-fabric/`.
- Route work to the owning product area or to prototyping rather than a generic root-level lane.

## Conventions

- {{Product vocabulary an agent must not guess at — acronyms, system names, stable identifiers. Keep this short; move large glossaries to a referenced doc.}}
- {{Optional: any team conventions worth stating — front-matter fields, writing style, review expectations. Keep only what the team actually follows.}}
